1
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:08,210
Jeez.

2
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:13,180
If you were done with work,
you could've just asked me to come over.

3
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,560
Hey.

4
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:24,060
Hey...

5
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,480
You were taking forever to call me,
so I just came over myself.

6
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:31,670
I even picked up some food on the way.

7
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:40,220
Hey...

8
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,560
You must be dying to hold me by now, right?

9
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:10,520
Well...

10
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:12,650
Takaaki, I'm starving.

11
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:14,750
Let's eat the bento I bought.

12
00:01:15,650 --> 00:01:16,650
Okay.

13
00:01:20,970 --> 00:01:22,970
Pepper steak or ginger pork.
Which one do you want?

14
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:24,579
You pick your favorite, Naoya.

15
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:26,030
Then I'll take the ginger pork.

16
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:43,020
Sorry.
I can never cook for you.

17
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,680
I don't have anything here.

18
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,600
It's fine.

19
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:49,580
You're always busy with work, right?

20
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:51,600
By the way,

21
00:01:51,610 --> 00:01:53,300
Have you been eating properly?

22
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,280
I guess so.

23
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:59,800
Whenever you come over,
you always make me super healthy meals.

24
00:02:00,950 --> 00:02:02,760
You should take better
care of yourself, too.

25
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:09,060
If you collapse from exhaustion,

26
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,350
I'd be in a lot of trouble.

27
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,330
Oh, right.

28
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:22,070
Want me to help you check
those documents after we eat?

29
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:23,360
I have tomorrow off anyway.

30
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:27,180
Sure, I'd appreciate that.

31
00:02:27,270 --> 00:02:28,770
No problem. Leave it to me.

32
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:40,420
But man,

33
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:43,550
this workload is insane.

34
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:46,760
You're handling all this by yourself?

35
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:49,310
I'm so glad you're helping me out.

36
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:57,480
I have no idea how you managed to
come to my place three times a week before.

37
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:04,760
Hey,

38
00:03:09,270 --> 00:03:10,840
should I just move in here?

39
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:17,860
Huh?

40
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
"The Servant Prince"
(Episode 6)

41
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:21,480
Should I just move in here?

42
00:04:25,090 --> 00:04:26,090
Huh?

43
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:30,910
Takaaki, you were the one who got that room
for me when I was completely broke, right?

44
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:37,620
If I cancel that lease and stay here,
I can help out with the living expenses.

45
00:04:38,230 --> 00:04:40,150
It would lighten your
burden a bit, wouldn't it?

46
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:43,280
Plus,

47
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:48,590
it'd be much easier for us
to find time to see each other.

48
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:03,060
Huh?

49
00:05:04,820 --> 00:05:05,820
Takaaki?

50
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:31,620
What?

51
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:34,100
This is...

52
00:05:35,410 --> 00:05:37,470
After selling the
apartment under your name,

53
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:41,780
and paying off the remaining mortgage, there
was still a substantial amount left over.

54
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:47,400
I actually could have gotten you
something much better than a studio.

55
00:05:50,430 --> 00:05:55,410
But ever since we were young, whenever you felt
vulnerable, you liked to hide in small spaces.

56
00:05:57,850 --> 00:05:58,850
That's right...

57
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:06,250
Just like how you used to curl up on the
sofa in the dimly lit computer club room.

58
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:11,130
A little box where you could heal.

59
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:17,850
A secret place
that only I knew about.

60
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:24,180
I was planning to give this to you
once you were back on your feet.

61
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:29,470
You can use this money
as capital to start a business.

62
00:06:29,900 --> 00:06:31,900
Or you could buy a new apartment.

63
00:06:33,390 --> 00:06:35,670
You don't need to worry at all
about being a burden to me.

64
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:42,870
Sorry for keeping this from you.

65
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,280
Heh.

66
00:06:55,330 --> 00:06:58,560
Looks like that apartment was worth
a lot more than I thought.

67
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:07,320
It's fine.

68
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:11,679
If you had given me that money back then,

69
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:13,240
it definitely wouldn't have ended well.

70
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:16,500
Yeah.

71
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:31,410
The rhythmic sound of typing
and Takaaki's back.

72
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:39,220
It's been like this for a long time.

73
00:07:45,210 --> 00:07:46,350
I'll think about it.

74
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:51,550
But until then,
can I still come over like this?

75
00:07:54,460 --> 00:07:56,570
Forget about the place or being a burden.

76
00:07:57,930 --> 00:07:59,370
I just want to see you more.

77
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:06,040
The thing that heals me the most

78
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:10,590
is always being by your side.

79
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:17,590
I was so lonely not seeing you for so long.

80
00:08:24,290 --> 00:08:25,830
What's with that look?

81
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:28,440
You've been really cute lately.

82
00:08:48,580 --> 00:08:49,830
You're welcome here anytime.

83
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:53,460
Thanks.

84
00:09:05,474 --> 00:09:10,334
[Some kind of dossier on Takaaki
including his performance as a young CEO)

85
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:18,390
Excuse me.

86
00:09:19,540 --> 00:09:20,540
President.

87
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:23,520
We got a reply from Unicolab
regarding the contract.

88
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:28,400
Hmph. With the amount we offered, they
must be wagging their tails in acceptance.

89
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:32,900
No, they formally declined.

90
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:34,250
What?

91
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:38,490
We made so many concessions.
What's the meaning of this?

92
00:09:38,570 --> 00:09:40,970
It doesn't seem to be
an issue with the quote.

93
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:43,010
Anyway, they said it's unacceptable.

94
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:55,300
Excuse me, President.

95
00:09:55,470 --> 00:09:57,470
Yuma, what is it?

96
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:01,400
Regarding the bidding for the
station-front development project,

97
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:02,939
are we really moving forward like this?

98
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:04,060
Obviously.

99
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:06,390
I'm busy.

100
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:08,850
Don't come running to
me for every little thing.

101
00:10:10,270 --> 00:10:11,520
I'm very sorry.

102
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:14,100
I'll take my leave.

103
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:41,340
Good morning.

104
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,310
Oh, Goto-kun.

105
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,720
- You're early today.
- Yes.

106
00:10:45,540 --> 00:10:46,540
Huh?

107
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:48,040
Is this a new dessert?

108
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:50,770
Yeah, I thought I'd try
changing the pancake mix.

109
00:10:50,980 --> 00:10:52,100
I used rice flour this time.

110
00:10:52,150 --> 00:10:53,399
It's what they call gluten-free.

111
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:54,690
I see.

112
00:10:55,900 --> 00:10:57,320
Smells great.

113
00:10:57,340 --> 00:10:58,630
- Looks delicious.
- Right?

114
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,110
By the way, Goto-kun,

115
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:02,240
if you don't mind,
want to give it a taste?

116
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,529
Oh, can I?

117
00:11:03,530 --> 00:11:05,040
Of course.

118
00:11:17,020 --> 00:11:18,020
It's delicious.

119
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:20,930
It's really chewy.
I actually prefer this one.

120
00:11:20,970 --> 00:11:22,050
Really?

121
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:23,600
That's great.

122
00:11:24,010 --> 00:11:25,140
This is really nice.

123
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:27,116
To think the head chef can
make something like this.

124
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:30,350
Come on, I've been a pro
in this industry for thirty years.

125
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,190
Thirty years, huh?

126
00:11:32,730 --> 00:11:34,610
I'm twenty-seven now,

127
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:36,659
so that's longer than I've been alive.

128
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:38,400
Hey, hold on a second.

129
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:40,070
Are you calling me an old man?

130
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:41,410
No, I didn't mean it like that.

131
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:43,660
I'm just kidding.

132
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:46,419
If you want to learn,
I can teach you the recipe.

133
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:48,830
It's actually pretty simple.
You can easily make it at home.

134
00:11:49,780 --> 00:11:50,540
Really?

135
00:11:50,541 --> 00:11:51,580
Of course.

136
00:11:56,220 --> 00:11:57,220
You're pretty handy.

137
00:11:57,780 --> 00:11:58,919
Do you cook often?

138
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,509
No, not at all.

139
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:03,340
Really? I couldn't tell.

140
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:07,076
You must be good with your hands.
You're probably great at everything.

141
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:08,380
Not at all.

142
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,020
Don't be modest.

143
00:12:10,770 --> 00:12:12,500
The manager and Mori-san said so, too.

144
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:16,120
They said even though you have no customer
service experience, you're incredibly adaptable.

145
00:12:16,240 --> 00:12:18,180
And you handle complaints flawlessly.

146
00:12:21,100 --> 00:12:22,380
That's because...

147
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:24,960
I guess a nepo baby
is just useless after all.

148
00:12:24,990 --> 00:12:27,490
Ruining your family's company.
You're completely worthless.

149
00:12:27,530 --> 00:12:29,290
You have zero management skills.

150
00:12:29,340 --> 00:12:30,620
You're an absolute disaster.

151
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:33,960
Because I used to be surrounded
by much worse people.

152
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:36,420
Huh?

153
00:12:38,050 --> 00:12:39,090
Oh, nothing.

154
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:42,159
It's done, it's done.

155
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:44,219
Oh, I see.

156
00:12:44,220 --> 00:12:45,469
See? Pretty simple, right?

157
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:46,350
Yes.

158
00:12:46,351 --> 00:12:49,640
Of course, we tweak it a bit for the store.

159
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:51,420
Like adding some whipped cream or fruit.

160
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:54,700
The rest is just professional technique.

161
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:56,480
Makes sense.

162
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:58,270
Anyway, that's the basic method.

163
00:12:58,320 --> 00:12:59,420
Thank you.

164
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:00,660
I'll definitely give it a try.

165
00:13:01,690 --> 00:13:03,690
By the way, who are you
learning to make this for?

166
00:13:03,930 --> 00:13:04,930
Ah...

167
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:07,660
- For a friend.
- A friend?

168
00:13:15,830 --> 00:13:16,850
Excuse me.

169
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:18,940
President.

170
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:20,960
I've brought him.

171
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:24,140
Long time no see,

172
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,300
President Goto.

173
00:13:25,660 --> 00:13:27,470
Thank you for always
looking after my father.

174
00:13:29,540 --> 00:13:33,140
I've already heard the gist of your visit
from your secretary, Tanizawa-san.

175
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:36,309
If it's about Unicolab,

176
00:13:36,310 --> 00:13:37,900
please leave it to me.

177
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:42,820
Their president, Sato Takaaki,
is a former classmate of mine.

178
00:14:12,086 --> 00:14:15,853
(I'm heading to the supermarket
first, I'll be over in a bit.)

179
00:14:39,250 --> 00:14:40,960
It really is Naoya.

180
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,520
This guy...

181
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:46,630
That's Naoya for you.

182
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:50,700
With Naoya here, we're definitely
winning the sports tournament.

183
00:14:51,430 --> 00:14:53,350
I'll follow you for life.
We're counting on you.

184
00:14:54,770 --> 00:14:55,850
Back in high school,

185
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:58,060
he was one of my lackeys, I think.

186
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:02,400
What a surprise.

187
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:05,780
I heard you hit rock bottom, but...

188
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:07,620
I never imagined

189
00:15:08,070 --> 00:15:10,730
you'd be running errands
for that four-eyes now.

190
00:15:16,910 --> 00:15:18,460
I've heard quite a bit.

191
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:24,040
Want me to put in a good word
and get you back into the company?

192
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:26,920
Get in.

193
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:39,890
You look pathetic.

194
00:15:40,730 --> 00:15:43,040
Dressed like a total bottom-feeder.

195
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:46,120
So?

196
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:48,820
Who told you to come here?

197
00:15:52,940 --> 00:15:54,040
Are you deaf?

198
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:57,040
I'm asking whose orders you're following.

199
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,080
You bastard.

200
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,770
Watch your attitude.

201
00:16:03,660 --> 00:16:06,040
You think you have the
right to question me?

202
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:09,530
If you think I'm still the same as before,
you're dead wrong.

203
00:16:10,420 --> 00:16:13,050
I've been sick of you since back then.

204
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:17,350
You're nothing but a guy who got
lucky being born as the president's son.

205
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:32,520
Whatever.

206
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:38,050
You must know about the data leak
at Goto Construction, right?

207
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:42,779
When I heard that four-eyes'
company was handling the security,

208
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:44,180
I was actually pretty shocked.

209
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:45,780
That guy...

210
00:16:45,830 --> 00:16:49,549
Even though he bailed halfway through,
we offered him a great deal to re-sign,

211
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:51,020
but he still wouldn't agree to it.

212
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:57,640
Your dad hasn't said anything publicly,
but it seems to be a real headache for him.

213
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:05,010
So I figured I'd step in as a mediator
and get things moving.

214
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:07,560
Oh.

215
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:14,670
Running into you here must be fate.

216
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:16,950
I might as well do you a favor, too.

217
00:17:17,910 --> 00:17:20,290
So watch your mouth.

218
00:17:24,670 --> 00:17:27,290
Why is it that the people around my father

219
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:30,560
always talk like this?

220
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:01,800
There's a meeting here tonight.

221
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:03,550
Wait in the lobby.

222
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:45,300
Am I too dressed-down for the moment?

223
00:19:06,590 --> 00:19:07,620
Sorry about that.

224
00:19:21,550 --> 00:19:22,949
Well, we should probably get going.

225
00:19:22,950 --> 00:19:24,080
Okay.

226
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:26,870
Say bye-bye.

227
00:19:27,330 --> 00:19:28,080
Bye-bye.

228
00:19:28,081 --> 00:19:29,670
- Bye-bye.
- See you next time.

229
00:19:30,570 --> 00:19:32,000
- Have a safe trip home.
- Yeah.

230
00:19:33,770 --> 00:19:35,750
- Let's go.
- Okay.

231
00:20:10,410 --> 00:20:11,500
Come with me.

232
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:32,400
(I'm going to the supermarket
first. I'll head over to your place later.)

233
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:34,370
He's still not back.

234
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:48,180
The number you dialed
is currently unavailable.

235
00:21:09,350 --> 00:21:10,490
I'll give you five minutes.

236
00:21:11,730 --> 00:21:13,229
If you get on your knees and apologize,

237
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:14,230
I'll forgive you.

238
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:20,530
All you have to do is say,

239
00:21:21,570 --> 00:21:24,660
"I can't do it," and bow your head to Dad.

240
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:26,820
He'll give you whatever position you want.

241
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:39,210
Come back.

242
00:21:40,190 --> 00:21:42,150
I can't hold on much longer all by myself.

243
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:55,240
I refuse.

244
00:22:01,750 --> 00:22:03,670
I have no intention of ever going back.

245
00:22:08,130 --> 00:22:09,570
That's what I came here to tell you.

246
00:22:14,710 --> 00:22:16,770
You're getting more and
more like your mother.

247
00:22:25,470 --> 00:22:26,680
You're going to regret this.

248
00:23:12,430 --> 00:23:14,970
The number you dialed
is currently unavailable.

249
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:31,776
(Next Episode Preview)
What are you doing?

250
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:32,800
Crap.

251
00:24:33,510 --> 00:24:34,470
Stop it, Takaaki!

252
00:24:34,471 --> 00:24:37,109
I have some exclusive
information about your son.

253
00:24:37,110 --> 00:24:38,149
So you guys are in this together?

254
00:24:38,150 --> 00:24:39,810
We'll be living here starting today.

255
00:24:39,850 --> 00:24:40,850
Just the two of us.
